.TH CONFUSB 1 "November 2026" "confusb 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
confusb \- USB device information and driver finder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B confusb
.RB [ \-\-devices ]
.RB [ \-\-show
.IR DEV ]
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.RB [ \-\-dump
.IR DEV ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B confusb
watches the USB connections. The first time a device is plugged in it offers to
show (with a notification, or by opening a window, depending on the settings)
all the information the system exposes about the device, and looks for its
driver and the applications needed to use it. Devices that are already known
do not show anything, and neither does a session that is not in the foreground
when several users are logged in. Storage drives are opened with the default
application for them (the file manager) once the system has mounted them.
.PP
It also asks the device itself for what sysfs and udev do not have: for an
Android phone with USB debugging enabled and authorized it reads, through
.BR adb (1),
the model, Android version, processor, memory, screen, battery and storage; for any
device it adds the full udev attribute tree.
.PP
Without arguments it runs as a service that watches the USB connections. It is
normally started automatically with the graphical session by the systemd user
unit
.IR confusb.service .
The service does not load the graphical toolkit and stays small. The windows
are a separate process: they are opened with
.B \-\-devices
or
.BR \-\-show ,
and the process ends, leaving the memory, when the last window is closed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-devices
Show the window with the connected USB devices.
.TP
.BI \-\-show " DEV"
Open the details of a device.
.I DEV
is a bus path such as
.IR 1\-5 ,
a
.I VID:PID
pair such as
.IR 058f:9540 ,
or a sysfs path.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the USB devices and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " DEV"
Print all the information of a device as text and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/confusb/ajustes.json
User settings (appearance of the cards, language and what to do when a device is
connected). They can be changed from the
.B Interface
button of the application.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/confusb/dispositivos.json
Devices that have already been connected (so that they are not offered again).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/confusb/avisos.json
Pending offers, passed from the service to the window.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The interface language is chosen in the application (language drop-down); by
default it follows the language of the desktop.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsusb (8),
.BR udevadm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
masebastia <https://github.com/masebastia/confusb>.
